gdxsv loopback binding patch for the private Online Mode backend.
Upstream: https://github.com/inada-s/gdxsv commit 46ee80b715f76ac0c7c254f6f983e5dcd9940306
License: AGPL-3.0 (this patch is distributed under the same license).

- main.go: the lobby and battle (MCS) listeners use the configured address
  instead of stripHost(), which upstream uses to bind all interfaces.
- main.go: the optional pprof listener binds 127.0.0.1 (backendctl also passes -pprof=0).
- lbs.go: the lobby UDP responder binds the lobby TCP host instead of all interfaces.
- loopback_bind_test.go: regression test; it fails on the pristine source
  because the lobby UDP responder answers on a non-loopback address.

- mcs_tcp.go and mcs_read_timeout.go: the battle peer read deadline (30 s
  upstream) can be raised with GDXSV_BATTLE_READ_TIMEOUT; unset keeps 30 s.
- mcs_read_timeout_test.go: regression test for that setting.

Apply from the source root with: patch -p1 --forward --batch < gdxsv-loopback.diff

